<!--
    The same mark the web app's favicon draws: a house with a play in it.

    Its comment there is the reason it is not YouTube's own rounded rectangle:
    that is a trademark rather than a layout, and the tokens read off YouTube's
    desktop are a reference for spacing and colour, its logo is not one of them.

    Drawn at 108dp with the shape inside the middle 66dp, which is what an
    adaptive icon reserves — the outer ring is cropped to whatever mask the
    launcher applies, and anything drawn there is lost on a round one.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
